<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consult-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consult-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consult-table.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ</span></nav><p class="kicker">Answers by topic</p><h1>Virginia Insurance Appraisal Questions, Answered</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers to the questions we hear most, grouped by topic: the basics, costs, timing, Virginia rules and working with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Topics"><p class="toc-h">Topics</p><ol><li><a href="#faq-0">Appraisal basics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-1">Costs &amp; fees</a></li><li><a href="#faq-2">Timing &amp; deadlines</a></li><li><a href="#faq-3">Virginia rules</a></li><li><a href="#faq-4">Working with us</a></li></ol></nav><h2 id="faq-0">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It’s a process written into most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers pick an umpire, and an award signed by two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not exactly. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss and is usually less formal than arbitration. It doesn’t decide coverage or legal claims.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can appraisal decide whether my damage is covered?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Generally no. Appraisers decide how much a loss costs. Whether something is covered is a legal question for the insurer, and if necessary a court, to decide.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most policies, either the policyholder or the insurer can demand it in writing once the two sides disagree on the amount of loss.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-1">Costs &amp; fees</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What does an appraiser cost?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Arrangements vary: flat fees, hourly rates or a percentage of the increase. We put our fee in writing before any work starts, and the first conversation is free.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who pays the umpire?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Most appraisal clauses split the umpire’s fee equally between you and the insurer. Each side pays its own appraiser.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal worth it on a small claim?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often not. When the gap is small, fees can absorb the recovery. A documented supplement request or an estimate review may close it more cheaply.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Timing &amp; deadlines</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many residential files finish within six to twelve weeks after both appraisers are named. Complex commercial files or umpire hearings take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal stop my deadline to sue?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not automatically. Some policies or agreements address it; many don’t. Track the suit-limitation date separately and talk to a Virginia attorney if it’s getting close.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long do I have to file suit in Virginia?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Virginia’s standard fire policy provisions commonly give two years from the date of loss, but your policy’s ‘Suit Against Us’ clause controls. Confirm the date with an attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>When should I demand appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>After the scope is fully documented and you have both estimates, but well before any policy deadline. Demanding too early is a common mistake.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Virginia rules</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance companies in Virginia?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Bureau of Insurance, part of the State Corporation Commission (SCC). It licenses insurers, agents and public adjusters and takes consumer complaints.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is the VPIA?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Virginia Property Insurance Association is Virginia’s FAIR Plan, a market of last resort for owners who can’t find property coverage in the voluntary market.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Virginia have a bad-faith law?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Virginia Code § 38.2-209 lets a court award a policyholder costs and reasonable attorney’s fees in certain cases where it finds an insurer denied coverage or refused to pay in bad faith. Section 38.2-510 lists unfair claim settlement practices the Bureau of Insurance enforces. These are legal matters for an attorney, not an appraiser.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is an appraiser the same as a public adjuster?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Public adjusters are licensed by the Bureau of Insurance to handle and negotiate claims for policyholders. An appraiser works within the appraisal clause on the amount of loss. We are not public adjusters.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What do you need from me to start?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Your declarations page, the insurer’s full estimate, any letters or emails, and photos. Your contractor’s estimate helps if you have one.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work outside the big cities?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We work statewide across Virginia’s 95 counties and 38 independent cities, from the Eastern Shore to Lee County.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you give legal advice?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. We’re not a law firm. If your claim involves a denial, a coverage question or a deadline that’s about to run, we’ll suggest you speak with a Virginia attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you guarantee a result?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No honest appraiser can. We can promise a careful, documented valuation and a straight answer about whether appraisal makes sense.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a><p class="box-small">Mon–Fri 8am–6pm ET · All of Virginia</p></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">Resources</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/virginia-appraisal-steps/">How appraisal works</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-appraisal-questions/" aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ</a></li><li><a href="/claim-and-policy-terms/">Claim &amp; policy terms</a></li><li><a href="/policy-and-claim-guides/">Claim guides</a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-strip-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email. We’re happy to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
